# OpenCode iOS port patch -- 0007
# Title: Node 18 iPhoneOS fallback compatibility (conditional variant)
# Upstream: anomalyco/opencode @ e8238bae9b807b72ecfc75afd3a9fe2e6b07b944 (v2.2.5)
# Requires: patches 0001-0006 applied first.
# Files: packages/cli/vite.node.config.ts
#        packages/cli/script/node-assets.ts
#        packages/core/src/provider.ts
#        packages/util/src/runtime/import.node.ts
#        packages/codemode/src/interpreter/objects.ts
# Why: conditional fallback for the device-proven Node 18.20.4 iPhoneOS runtime (used as a hedge
#      while the Node 22.9 runtime's JIT/wasm support is being fixed). Selected by
#      OPENCODE_IOS_NODE18=1 at build time; the default Node 22 variant is unchanged. Changes:
#      - Node 18 prelude: defines __filename/__dirname from import.meta.url (Node 18 has no
#        import.meta.filename/dirname), global crypto, and the missing built-ins
#        (Array.toSorted/toReversed/toSpliced/with/findLast*, Object.groupBy, Map.groupBy,
#        Promise.withResolvers, Array.fromAsync, String.isWellFormed/toWellFormed, AbortSignal.any);
#        the shebang/launcher flags avoid --experimental-sqlite and --disable-warning (newer Node).
#        Vite build target becomes node18.
#      - node:sqlite is mapped to a sql.js-backed synchronous shim (port file
#        src/opencode-ios/node18-sqlite-shim.mjs) that implements the DatabaseSync/StatementSync
#        subset this tree uses; the build script stages sql.js JS+wasm (pinned tarball sha256) as
#        assets/node18-sqlite/.
#      - vm.constants.USE_MAIN_CONTEXT_DEFAULT_LOADER fallback (absent before Node 20.12) for
#        plugin entrypoint imports; plain dynamic import is used instead.
#      - Iterator-helper-free mergeRecord and codemode Map/URLSearchParams/Headers iterators:
#        Node 18 lacks Iterator.prototype.map and Iterator.from.
# Test: OPENCODE_IOS_NODE18=1 bash scripts/build-opencode-bundle.sh build stage smoke manifest
#       (required host smoke Node 18.20.4; Node 22.9.0 informational).
#       Host evidence and device-risk notes: docs/OPENCODE_BUILD.md section 13.
# Status: conditional hedge variant; the default Node 22 artifact path is not changed.

